# Pretty URLs — Netlify-style rewrites the IPFS gateway applies for DNSLink /
# subdomain hosts (enclave.host serves via DNSLink; docs: specs.ipfs.tech/http-
# gateways/web-redirects-file). Rules are evaluated ONLY for paths that do not
# exist in the DAG, so the shipped .html files keep serving at their old URLs
# (the router's history.replaceState canonicalizes those in the address bar).
# Ships from the site root via build-site.mjs; nan-deploy.sh pins it with -r.
/apps       /apps.html       200
/develop    /develop.html    200
/dashboard  /dashboard.html  200
/checkout   /checkout.html   200
/link       /link.html       200
/authorize  /authorize.html  200
# tenant-app sign-in (Sign in with Enclave): a NESTED document so it can
# coexist with /authorize above (the private-app hand-off) - boot.js pageOf
# keys it as "sso-authorize" from the parent segment
/sso/authorize /sso/authorize.html 200
/host       /host.html       200
/admin      /admin.html      200
/terms      /terms.html      200
/privacy    /privacy.html    200
# /apps/publish is a VIEW of the Apps page (a router alias): a hard load
# serves the nested apps document (a build-time copy carrying <base
# href="../">) and apps.js picks the view from the pathname. The flat /publish
# form stays as a rewrite to the ROOT-DEPTH document (no base needed there);
# the router canonicalizes the bar to the nested form.
/apps/publish  /apps/publish.html  200
/publish       /apps.html          200
# the old deploy console (/apps/deploy, and the older /deploy) is gone: an app
# deploys from its card in the store, and every setting the console carried
# is a tab on the deployment's dashboard row. Old links land on the store.
# deploy.html stays only as the legacy /deploy.html redirect stub.
/apps/deploy   /apps/   301
/deploy        /apps/   301
# Everything else absent from the DAG: the branded 404 page with a real 404
# status (404.html carries <base href="/"> because it serves AT the missing
# path). Absent OLD chunk hashes now serve this HTML instead of the gateway
# error page - module loading fails identically either way (skew-heal covers
# the mixed-edge window), so the union-archive protection is unaffected.
/* /404.html 404
